{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791122163,"nonce":"GKOoTE8Zvi+XxFHuz73eBDKt0So=","title":"line_height is read as a multiple of the face's natural line height, not the font size","message":"TextMeasureContext.line_height is treated as a multiple of the face's\nown line height (ascent + descent + line gap) in both measurement and\nrendering. CSS's line-height is a multiple of the font size.\n\nWith Helvetica, where ascent + descent is 1em, the two agree, which is\nwhy this has not shown up. With SF Pro or Inter every line comes out\nabout 19 to 21 percent taller than CSS would make it.\n\nThe ashui session converts in its binding, storing css / natural so the\nmeasured line is font_size * css. Blinc may want CSS semantics natively,\nwhich would change measured heights for any face whose natural line\nheight is not 1em, so it is a visible layout change rather than a\ncontained fix.","files":null}]}